  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "If $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are polynomials of degree $11$ and $10$, respectively, the degree of $P+Q$ is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Since $P$ is a polynomial of degree $11,$ the leading term contains an ${x}^{11}.$\n\nSince $Q$ is a polynomial of degree $10,$ the leading term contains an ${x}^{10}.$\n\nIn $P+Q,$ the highest-order term still contains an ${x}^{11}.$ No ${x}^{11}$ term in $P$ could possibly cancel out the ${x}^{11}$ term in $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the degree of $P+Q$ must be $11.$",
